{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-468445-r4541102","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Rujak Cingur (Indonesian Cow Snout Salad)","sourcePageId":468445,"sourceRevision":"4541102","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-04T23:10:52Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Rujak%20Cingur%20(Indonesian%20Cow%20Snout%20Salad)&oldid=4541102","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:46:28.288Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Indonesian recipes","Category:Javanese recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bean sprout","Category:Recipes using beef","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cucumber","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using palm sugar","Category:Recipes using peanut","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using salt","Category:Recipes using tamarind","Category:Recipes using tofu","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Tempeh recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4f23f9a19ca03141b40300e8c9be314742358e43ddced531ca4d27e87d0bf2a3","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Indonesian recipes\n| Servings = 1\n| Image = [[File:Rujak Cingur.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\n'''Rujak cingur''' is a traditional food from Surabaya, Indonesia. This dish is made from ''cingur'' (cow's snout) and vegetables, which are drizzled with peanut sauce or petis sauce.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Sauce ===\n\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] fried [[Cookbook:Peanut|peanuts]]\n* 2 cloves of fried [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 3 bird’s eye [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]], or to taste\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Palm Sugar|palm sugar]]\n* ½ teaspoon terasi [[Cookbook:Shrimp Paste|shrimp paste]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 tablespoons of petis [[Cookbook:Shrimp Paste|shrimp paste]]\n* [[Cookbook:Tamarind|Tamarind]] water as needed\n\n=== Assembly ===\n\n* 100 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] boiled or fried cow’s snout (cingur)\n* 1 bunch of [[Cookbook:Water Spinach|water spinach]] (kangkung), leaves picked and boiled\n* 100 grams boiled [[Cookbook:Bean Sprout|bean sprouts]] (taoge)\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cucumber|cucumber]], [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n* 1 slice of fried [[Cookbook:Tempeh|tempeh]]\n* 1 slice of fried [[Cookbook:Tofu|tofu]]\n* 1 ''lontong'' rice cake, cut into pieces as desired\n* 250 grams ''kerupuk'' crackers\n\n== Procedure ==\n\n# Prepare all the ingredients in advance.\n# To make the sauce, grind the fried peanuts, garlic, chiles, palm sugar, terasi, and salt together until smooth.\n# Add the petis suace and tamarind water as needed. Mix until well blended.\n# Arrange all the ingredients for assembly onto a serving plate, starting with the cingur, then water spinach, bean sprouts, cucumber, tempeh, tofu, and rice cake.\n# Drizzle the sauce over the ingredients, and top with the crackers.\n\n[[Category:Javanese recipes]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using peanut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tamarind]]\n[[Category:Recipes using beef]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bean sprout]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cucumber]]\n[[Category:Tempeh recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tofu]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using palm sugar]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Rujak Cingur (Indonesian Cow Snout Salad)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"1","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 tablespoons fried peanuts","sourceText":"2 tablespoons fried peanuts","amountText":"2 tablespoons fried peanuts","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cloves of fried garlic","sourceText":"2 cloves of fried garlic","amountText":"2 cloves of fried garlic","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 bird’s eye chiles, or to taste","sourceText":"3 bird’s eye chiles, or to taste","amountText":"3 bird’s eye chiles, or to taste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 tablespoon palm sugar","sourceText":"1 tablespoon palm sugar","amountText":"1 tablespoon palm sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ teaspoon terasi shrimp paste","sourceText":"½ teaspoon terasi shrimp paste","amountText":"½ teaspoon terasi shrimp paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"½ teaspoon salt","sourceText":"½ teaspoon salt","amountText":"½ teaspoon salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"2 tablespoons of petis shrimp paste","sourceText":"2 tablespoons of petis shrimp paste","amountText":"2 tablespoons of petis shrimp paste","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"Tamarind water as needed","sourceText":"Tamarind water as needed","amountText":"Tamarind water as needed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"100 grams boiled or fried cow’s snout (cingur)","sourceText":"100 grams boiled or fried cow’s snout (cingur)","amountText":"100 grams boiled or fried cow’s snout (cingur)","a